+   // pack: main thread caught mid-lookup during a live TPS dip). GameRules.getBoolean()
+   // does a Guava ImmutableMap hash lookup on every single call even though the
+   // underlying BooleanValue object's IDENTITY never changes for a given (Level, Key)
+   // pair — only its internal boolean mutates in place via /gamerule.
+   //
+   // Single-slot cache instead of a map: a server has a handful of Level instances
+   // (one per dimension) that live for the server's whole lifetime, and call patterns
+   // are heavily repetitive for the SAME Level in a row (this exact loop, one chunk's
+   // worth of fluid positions at a time) — a map (even a fast one) is pure overhead
+   // next to a single reference comparison. nestworldCache is a single volatile
+   // pointer to an IMMUTABLE {level, value} pair, swapped atomically on a miss: any
+   // thread that reads it always sees a fully-consistent pair (never a torn read
+   // where one thread observes a level from one update and a value from another,
+   // which two SEPARATE volatile fields would risk under concurrent access from
+   // different region threads generating different dimensions at once). A race on
+   // the miss path just means one thread's freshly-built entry overwrites another's —
+   // both are correct, it only costs an extra GameRules lookup, never a wrong answer.
+   // NestWorld: package-private (not private) so LavaFluid.randomTick/canConvertToSource
+   // can reuse this same small immutable pair type instead of duplicating it.
+   static final class NestworldGameRuleCacheEntry {
+      final Level level;
+      final GameRules.BooleanValue value;
+      NestworldGameRuleCacheEntry(Level level, GameRules.BooleanValue value) {
